dist/
.env

# Contains real traffic, conversion counts and modelled pipeline.
# data.example/ is committed instead, same shapes, fabricated numbers.
data/
*.local.json

# Every real config, whatever the product is called this week.
#
# This was `rainmaker.config.yml` alone, and before that `paydirt.config.yml`.
# Renaming the product renamed the ignore rule, the file on disk kept its old
# name, and it silently became trackable: a config with a real site, ICP, GSC
# property and booking link was committed by a `git add -A` that had no reason
# to warn about it. Match the shape instead of the name so a future rename
# cannot quietly unprotect anything.
#
# `*.config.example.yml` does not match this pattern and stays committed.
*.config.yml
